---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site, mailLink, waLink, quoteMessage } from "../data/site";
import { getSitePage, REVIEWED_DATE, REVIEWED_ISO } from "../data/sitePages";

const page = getSitePage("/contact/");
---

<BaseLayout
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  alternateMd="/contact/index.md"
  pageType="WebPage"
  dateModified={REVIEWED_ISO}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Contact" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Contact us</h1>
      <p class="small">Last reviewed: {REVIEWED_DATE}</p>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--ink-2)">
        Talk to the quotation and quality-control team by email or WhatsApp. We answer questions about labels,
        materials, artwork and shipping; we do not act as your lawyer, customs broker or regulatory adviser.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin:24px 0">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Email</h3>
          <p><a href={mailLink("Quotation request — custom labels and stickers")}>{site.email}</a></p>
          <p class="small">Best for specifications, artwork files, document requests and anything you need in writing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>WhatsApp</h3>
          <p><a href={waLink(quoteMessage)} rel="noopener">{site.whatsappDisplay}</a></p>
          <p class="small">Best for a quick question, a container photo or an order-status check.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What we can answer</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Whether a label size, shape or material is practical for your container and quantity.</li>
        <li>How artwork, bleed, colour, proofs and samples work before production.</li>
        <li>What changes a price, what the minimum order covers and what information the quotation needs.</li>
        <li>Production, packing, shipping, tracking and the documents we can request from a producer.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we cannot answer</h2>
      <p>
        We cannot provide legal advice, a binding customs classification ruling, regulatory approval for a product
        or market, or a guarantee that a retailer or marketplace will accept a label. We can explain what we print
        and what documentation can be requested, but your importer, regulatory adviser and customs broker must make
        those decisions. A question outside our competence gets an honest “we do not know” rather than a confident
        guess.
      </p>

      <h2>What to include in a first message</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Input</th><th scope="col">What helps us answer</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Product and use</td><td>Label, sticker or hang tag; the container, surface or packaging it goes on</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Size and quantity</td><td>Width and height in mm, or diameter, plus quantity per design and the number of designs</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Material and finish</td><td>Paper, PP, PET, vinyl or “recommend one”; gloss, matte, foil or another finish if required</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Destination</td><td>Country and postcode, so the quote can state a realistic shipping option</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Artwork and timing</td><td>Whether the file is ready, what it needs to meet, and the date you need the goods</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        A photo of the container is often more useful than a finished design. If you do not know the material, say so:
        choosing it is part of the conversation, not a prerequisite for asking.
      </p>

      <h2>Response times and languages</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to acknowledge an enquiry within <strong>1 business day</strong>, Monday to Friday, China Standard Time
        (GMT+8). Artwork checks, producer documents and samples can need a second reply; we will give you the next
        expected date rather than leave the request open. We answer in English. If you send another language, we may
        use a translation tool and will confirm the specification in English before quoting.
      </p>

      <h2>Samples, documents and verification</h2>
      <p>
        Physical samples can be requested before a full run; cost and timing are quoted with the job. Document
        requests are acknowledged within 2 business days under the <a href="/declarations/">declarations process</a>.
        Before paying, you can verify the legal entity through China's public registry and Dun &amp; Bradstreet using
        the links on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>, and check the invoice name. Banking details appear only on
        the invoice for a confirmed order.
      </p>

      <h2>Before you send</h2>
      <p>
        Do not send card numbers, online-banking passwords or government identity documents. Tell us before sharing
        a confidential artwork pack if you need an NDA; we will confirm whether we can accept its terms before you
        upload the files. If payment instructions in an email differ from the invoice, stop and call the number on
        the invoice before paying.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        Read <a href="/request-a-quote/">how to request a quote</a>, <a href="/shipping-delivery/">shipping</a>,
        <a href="/terms/">terms</a> and <a href="/privacy/">privacy</a>. Related policies:
        <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> · <a href="/refund-policy/">Returns</a> ·
        <a href="/declarations/">Declarations</a> · <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial standards</a> ·
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> · <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a> ·
        <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
